From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FramePlayer contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] xr: antialiasing for Linux OpenXR pages

XRWebGLLayer antialias was always false on the Steam Frame: the OpenXR
device offers antialiasing only when the runtime's
maxSwapchainSampleCount is above 1, and SteamVR reports 1. That limit is
about rendering into the swapchain itself, which Linux never does:
pages draw into a SharedImage that XRWebGLDrawingBuffer resolves before
the Vulkan binding copies it into the swapchain. Pages tuned on Quest,
whose browser renders them with MSAA, looked jagged and shimmered.

On Linux, CanEnableAntiAliasing() is always true. Patch 0013 makes Blink
use 2 samples on Linux arm64. With ANGLE on Vulkan, Blink's implicit
resolve (GL_EXT_multisampled_render_to_texture) never reached the
headset, so the Frame launcher disables that extension and Blink
resolves with a blit.

Touches only device/vr/openxr/openxr_view_configuration.cc, which no
other patch changes.
---
diff --git a/device/vr/openxr/openxr_view_configuration.cc b/device/vr/openxr/openxr_view_configuration.cc
index d88ba5627f..9c0c4c1f2d 100644
--- a/device/vr/openxr/openxr_view_configuration.cc
+++ b/device/vr/openxr/openxr_view_configuration.cc
@@ -305,6 +305,13 @@ void OpenXrViewConfiguration::SetViews(std::vector<XrView> views) {
 }
 
 bool OpenXrViewConfiguration::CanEnableAntiAliasing() const {
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX)
+  // Linux pages always draw into a SharedImage that Blink resolves itself
+  // (XRWebGLDrawingBuffer) before the Vulkan binding copies it into the
+  // swapchain, so the runtime's swapchain sample count doesn't limit it.
+  // SteamVR reports 1, which left every page without antialiasing.
+  return true;
+#else
   // From the OpenXR Spec:
   // maxSwapchainSampleCount is the maximum number of sub-data element samples
   // supported for swapchain images that will be rendered into for this view.
@@ -314,6 +321,7 @@ bool OpenXrViewConfiguration::CanEnableAntiAliasing() const {
   return std::ranges::all_of(properties_, [](const OpenXrViewProperties& view) {
     return view.MaxSwapchainSampleCount() > 1;
   });
+#endif
 }
 
 }  // namespace device
